    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "With **IMPERIAL KNIGHTS** as your [Army Faction](vsdata:core-rule/select-army-faction), once Read Mission Objectives is over, you have to set the Oath your army takes into the battle. An Oath has 2 parts, a Deed and a Quality, with 3 options for each, listed below. For each part, pick an option, or roll a D6 on its table to pick one at random. Your Deed says what has to be achieved to complete it. Your Quality's ability applies to every model of yours with this ability for the rest of the battle.\n\nYour Oath is fulfilled the first time you complete its Deed: your army is Honoured for the rest of the battle, and you gain 3CP if you picked your Deed or Quality, or both, at random, or 2CP if not. These CP are an exception to the Core Rules limit of 1CP gained per battle round.\n\n**Deeds**:\n\n- **We vow to lay low the tyrant...** (1-2): as the battle begins, pick a **CHARACTER** model from your opponent's army. The Deed is completed as a turn ends if that model has been **destroyed**.\n- **We swear to reclaim the realm...** (3-4): the Deed is completed as your opponent's turn ends if your opponent controls fewer [objective markers](vsdata:core-rule/objectives) than you.\n- **We pledge to reap a great tally...** (5-6): the Deed is completed as a battle round ends if more enemy units were destroyed in that battle round than its number, even ones that later return to the battlefield; in battle round 1, for example, 2 are enough.\n\n**Qualities**:\n\n- **...with all our martial valour risen over all.** (1-2): whenever this model gets **selected to shoot** or **selected to fight**, you get to re-roll a [Hit roll](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls) and a [Wound roll](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls) for it.\n- **...and we are eager for the challenge.** (3-4): this model gets +2\" M and +1 to its [Advance](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) and [Charge rolls](vsdata:core-rule/charge-step).\n- **...yet shall our legacy be unsullied.** (5-6): this model gets +2 OC and +1 Ld.",
